  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "2Z8Dvu/SCZWMO2XkFu06pSvgybc=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:35.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## The canonical shape\n\n`generate` is built with cmd-ts `subcommands({ name: \"generate\", cmds: { ... } })`. Seven subcommands, exactly:\n\n`all` \u00b7 `document-model` \u00b7 `editor` \u00b7 `app` \u00b7 `processor` \u00b7 `subgraph` \u00b7 `migration-file`\n\nThere is **no flag-driven form**. `ph generate --editor`, `--processor`, `--subgraph`, `--drive-editor`, and `ph generate <file>.phd` are all dead; `app` is the replacement for the retired `--drive-editor` generator. Verified live forms:\n\n```bash\nph generate all\nph generate document-model --document TodoList.phd      # -d; .phd or .json\nph generate editor        --name MyEditor --document-type my-org/todo\nph generate app           --name MyApp --document-types my-org/todo,my-org/note\nph generate processor     --name Stats --type analytics --document-types my-org/todo\nph generate subgraph      --name mySubgraph\nph generate migration-file --path ./migrations/001.ts\n```\n\n## Flag details that bite\n\n`editor` takes **singular `--document-type` / `-t`**; `app` and `processor` take **plural `--document-types` / `-t=`** (repeatable or comma-separated). Getting the plurality wrong is the most common failure.\n\n`processor` also takes `--type` (default `analytics`) and `--apps` (default `switchboard,connect` \u2014 whether the processor runs in Node, the browser, or both). `app` has `--disable-drag-and-drop` (default `false`).\n\n`migration-file` is the odd one out: no `--name`, and `--path` is **required**, with `--schema-file` defaulting to `./schema.ts`.\n\n## Three axes per subcommand\n\nEvery module subcommand supports the same triple:\n\n- **Create new** \u2014 `--name` plus type flags, or `--document <spec.phd|.json>` to drive codegen from a Vetra spec document.\n- **Re-generate existing** \u2014 `--dir <dir>` for one module, `--all` / `-a` for every module of that kind.\n- **Extract** \u2014 `--extract` / `-x` inverts the command: instead of generating code it writes a spec document for each existing module into `specs/<kind>/`.\n\n`generate all` carries only `--extract`; it otherwise re-generates every module in the project.\n\n_Source: `clis/ph-cli/src/commands/generate.ts` plus the seven `generate-*.ts` siblings, mirrored in `apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/07-CLITooling/00-PowerhouseCLI.md`, Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:35.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:35.000Z"
    }
  },
